WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.322
Here is what an app actually costs to build

2
00:00:02.473 --> 00:00:04.435
— no email, no wizard,

3
00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:07.465
no waiting. Start with platforms.

4
00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.519
Both iOS and Android is the normal answer,

5
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.423
because we ship both from one build,

6
00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:14.234
so it does not double your price.

7
00:00:14.838 --> 00:00:17.322
Next, pick the kind of app you are describing.

8
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.922
Simple is a few screens with no accounts.

9
00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:22.024
Standard adds user accounts,

10
00:00:22.198 --> 00:00:24.264
saved data and notifications.

11
00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:27.132
Now tick the features you are fairly sure about.

12
00:00:27.573 --> 00:00:29.849
Watch the number on the right — it updates

13
00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:32.055
the moment you click, and the list underneath

14
00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:34.481
tells you exactly which of your answers moved

15
00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:37.523
it. Payments and chat move it the most.

16
00:00:37.848 --> 00:00:40.170
Accounts and push barely move it at all.

17
00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:43.224
You also get a build timeline in weeks and

18
00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:45.558
a suggested Care plan for after launch.

19
00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.856
One click copies the whole estimate to your

20
00:00:47.903 --> 00:00:50.132
clipboard. Nothing is uploaded,

21
00:00:50.248 --> 00:00:52.419
nothing is stored, and when you are ready the

22
00:00:52.465 --> 00:00:54.799
brief locks the scope and the price in.
